From 211f01ea281dfbd9957e733ba76222838ea10bd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:55:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/25] time: Follow POSIX.1-2024 in strptime

- Numeric conversions read no more than their maximum width, or the
  given field width, so "%Y%m%d" works; the 0 and + flags are
  accepted and ignored.
- %C and %y combine; %y alone maps 69 to 1969, not 2069.
- %a and %A accept full and abbreviated names, as do %b, %B and %h.
- %F takes a year of any width, limited by a field width.
- %Z reads a name and sets tm_isdst when it matches tzname; %z, %G
  and %g are parsed.
- tm_isdst is no longer set to -1, which POSIX doesn't allow.
